Return `false` explicitly from the `_.transform` iteratee to stop iteration early. The iteratee receives `(accumulator, value, key, object)`.

```js
_.transform(object, function (accumulator, value, key, object) {
  if (shouldStop(value)) {
    return false; // exits iteration
  }

  accumulator[key] = value;
}, {});
```

`_.transform` is intended for accumulating into an object or array; returning `false` exits the iteration rather than replacing the accumulator.
